econdary_8", "content": " Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn5le06ob04re1img01.png"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Sentence Stress"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Sentence stress gives English its <span class =\"strong\">rhythm</span> or \"beat\"."}, {"type": "text", "content": " Word stress is emphasis on <span class =\"strong\">one syllable</span> within a <span class =\"strong\">word</span>.  "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Sentence stress is emphasis on <span class =\"strong\">certain words</span> within a <span class =\"strong\">sentence</span>.  "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Most sentences have two basic types of words:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class =\"strong\">Content words </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul>  \t<li>Content words are the important or key words of a sentence.<br /> They provide the meaning of the sentence.</li> </ul>   \t\t\t"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class =\"strong\">Structure words </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul>  \t<li>Structure words are not important words.<br /> They are small words that you use to make the sentence correct.</li> </ul>   \t\t\t"}, {"type": "text", "content": " Placing the stress on the wrong syllable in a word or placing stress on the wrong word in a sentence may lead to confusion or loss of meaning."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "hunk "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an attractive man "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Vanessa thinks that Marco is a hunk."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le06ob04aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use when talking about relationships."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to drool "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to show admiration or desire for something or someone in an exaggerated way "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: She was drooling over him."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le06ob04aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "well-traveled "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a person who has traveled a lot"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Marco is very well-traveled."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le06ob04aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "naive "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "having or showing a lack of experience or knowledge "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Vanessa is so naive when it comes to guys."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le06ob04aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "charmer "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "someone who can convince other of their skills and abilities "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Marco is such a charmer."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le06ob04aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "love them and leave them "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "not staying in a relationship for a long time "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Marco is a love them and leave them kind of guy."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le06ob04aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "a lot in common "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to have similar interests "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expre